# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# <footer>

# COMMIT TYPES
# feat:     A new feature
# fix:      A bug fix
# docs:     Documentation only changes
# style:    Changes that do not affect the meaning of the code (formatting, missing semicolons, etc)
# refactor: A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
# perf:     A code change that improves performance
# test:     Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
# chore:    Changes to the build process, dependencies, tooling, or configuration
# ci:       Changes to CI configuration files and scripts

# SCOPES (examples)
# ios-app, streaming-server, docker, config, documentation
# playback, ui, network, error-handling, architecture

# SUBJECT LINE RULES
# - Use imperative, present tense: "change" not "changed" or "changes"
# - Don't capitalize first letter
# - No period (.) at the end
# - Limit to 50 characters
# - Reference issues and breaking changes

# BODY RULES (optional)
# - Wrap at 72 characters
# - Use imperative, present tense
# - Include motivation for the change
# - Explain what and why, not how
# - Separate from subject line with a blank line

# FOOTER RULES (optional)
# - Reference issue tracker IDs (e.g., Closes #123)
# - Note breaking changes with "BREAKING CHANGE:"

# EXAMPLES
# --------
# feat(playback): add play/pause controls
#
# Implement pause button and play state toggling in VideoPlayerView.
# - Add pause() method to PlaybackViewModel
# - Create UI controls in VideoPlayerView
# - Update debug panel to show current state
#
# Closes #42

# --------
# fix(streaming): resolve HLS segment loading timeout
#
# Increase timeout from 2s to 3s to handle slower networks.
# This fixes buffering issues on cellular connections.

# --------
# docs: update DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE with new machine steps
#
# Add step-by-step guide for deploying to Raspberry Pi.

# --------
# refactor(viewmodel): simplify error handling logic
#
# Extract repeated error handling into separate method.
# Makes code more maintainable and testable.

# --------
# chore: update Swift formatting in .editorconfig
#
# Ensure consistent 4-space indentation across all editors.
